      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Clinical trials demonstrate that cardiovascular event rates diminish as low-density lipoprotein (LDL)-cholesterol and apolipoprotein B-containing particles are lowered with statin treatment. The relationship between LDL-cholesterol and cardiovascular events seems to be linear, with no lowest threshold. While LDL-cholesterol remains the primary target for coronary heart disease prevention, non-HDL-cholesterol is an important secondary target in patients with mixed dyslipidemia."},
